+5|//! `dot: true` configuration and evaluates the result with `fancy_regex`
+6|//! (needed for the lookaheads picomatch emits).
+7|//!
+8|//! The structure deliberately mirrors `lib/parse.js`: the tokenizer appends 
to
+9|//! `state.output` as it goes, but several rules retroactively rewrite the
+10|//! output of an already-emitted token (`push`'s globstar downgrade, the 
`**`
+11|//! lookarounds, the literal-bracket fallback). Reproducing that 
back-patching
+12|//! is what makes the emitted source byte-identical to picomatch's, which
+13|//! `tests/picomatch.rs` asserts against a recorded oracle.
