`"a/"` exp true got false; `"a**{[[:alpha:]]@(a|b)"`. Verified empirically in 
JS: `"[]/a"` → `^(?:\[\]\/a\/?)$`, and token dump shows a single `bracket` token
`'[\\]/a{a,b}'` consuming the `/` (brackets-left output 
`"\\\\[^/]*?\\[\\]/a{a,b}\\/?"`).
  3. **`$^` fallback missing**: JS `picomatch.toRegex` wraps `new RegExp(...)` 
in try/catch and returns `/$^/` on invalid regex (picomatch.js:326). Rust 
returns the malformed source instead. Evidence: `"[^a](@(a|b){1..3"` exp 
`Some("$^")` got `Some("^(?:[^a/]((a|b)\\(1\\..3\\})$")`; also `"{"` and 
`"a**{[[:alpha:]]@(a|b)"` expect `$^`.
